{{Term/Store|Midna's Helmet|Midna's Helmets|Series, BotW, TotK}} is a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
Midna's Helmet is a piece of [[Armor]] that [[Link]] can wear on his head. It is exclusive to {{TMT}} [[Downloadable Content]] pack. The bandit [[Misko]] stole it from [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]], along with several other treasures.<ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/> During the "[[EX Treasure: Twilight Relic]]" [[Side Quest]], Link is tasked with reading ''[[Misko's EX Journal 2]]'' in order to learn the location of Midna's Helmet.<ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/> In reading it, he discovers that the Helmet can be found at the ruins of a temple flooded by the [[Regencia River]].<ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal"/> At the [[Sage Temple Ruins]], Link will find a [[Hidden Chest]] embedded in the ground, which contains Midna's Helmet.<ref name="BotW Adventure Log 2"/> Midna's Helmet grants both [[Guardian Resist Up]] and [[Ancient Pow Up]].

Once acquired, [[Granté]] will begin selling Midna's Helmet for 50 [[Rupee]]s.{{Note|Prior to the [[The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild#Updates|Version 1.3.3 Update]], Granté would not sell any Armor that is exclusive to the ''[[Breath of the Wild Expansion Pass]]''. This meant that Midna's Helmet could not be replaced if sold, which was noted in its [[Inventory]] description.<ref name="BotW Inventory 2"/>}} Furthermore it cannot be [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] or enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]].

